# Sources used:
# - French Wikipedia, Bouyon (musique) article, Rekenteng section (read via search result quoting the page, 2026-10-20): "Parmi les premiers groupes et crews ayant joue un role essentiel dans la popularisation du Rekenteng figurent le Bushtown Clan, Klockerz Krew et Nursery Crew Ink"; the style described as built on sampling, mixing popular hip hop and dancehall anthems with aggressive bouyon drum programming; emblematic examples given by that page: bouyon remixes of "Big Pimpin'" by Jay-Z with UGK and "Ridin' Dirty" by Chamillionaire, presented as founding classics. The same page flags part of the surrounding section as needing a reference, so every claim from it is attributed in this profile.
# - This site's own spelling law: the official spelling is "Wrecketeng", given by DJ Cut himself; "reketeng" is the spelling used by the French Wikipedia page and across the internet, flagged in this profile as the internet misspelling. Bouyon soca origin context follows the site record: started by Dada in Dominica in 2003 per Smokiller first-hand testimony, popularized by Triple Kay.
# - A Virtual Dominica, Music from Dominica page (opened 2026-10-20): "Born Dennison Ikes Joseph, better known as 'Dice', first began singing R n' B and reggae in the 90's music group Klockerz Crew"; Dice calypso path: first Carnival Calypso competition 2002 (quarter final), third place 2003, Calypso King 2004, eight crowns in total per that page.
# - Caribbean Times (read via search result, 2026-10-20): reporting Trilla G's calypso monarch win, the paper calls Dennison "Dice" Joseph a nine-time calypso monarch who placed second that year. The eight versus nine count difference between the two sources is stated openly in this profile.
# - Skydimex artist biography, published artist bio text reproduced on biography aggregator pages (read 2026-10-20, used with attribution as a self published artist bio): member of the Klockerz crew, started his career at 18; the crew explored a mix of dancehall, hip hop and soca (bouyon); three albums, Mental of Instrumental, K2 and Sign'O'The Times, and a live album; opening acts for Kassav', Buju Banton, Sanchez and TOK; in 2009 Skydimex moved solo to Guadeloupe, working with Mad JMC (one of Krys' producers), ManDragon and OneTime studio.
# - Shazam, "Tonite a De Nite" by Partners In Kryme (opened 2026-10-20): performing artists Partners In Kryme and Skinny Banton; credits name Klockerz as composer and Skinny Banton as songwriter; the track appears on the compilation "200% Soca, 100% Tubes, Vol. 2", Pastel Productions, listed as released January 1, 2002, at 149 BPM. An older Wikipedia bouyon bands list also carried Partners In Kryme among the old school bouyon bands.
# Note: THIN DOSSIER. No official page, no verified member list, no album dates and no official social profile of the crew were found during research. No link is made in sameAs and only one streaming era recording credit could be verified.

